---
import AppLandingPage from '../../components/AppLandingPage.astro';
import { LEARNING_APPS } from '../../data/apps';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Which boating licence app is best?',
    a: 'It depends on what you need. For the widest licence coverage plus a companion online course, Bootspruefung.de is the safe pick. If you are taking a single licence and do not want to spend anything, the free apps by Matthias Wimmer are the best choice. If you want to book theory and practice as a package, look at Bootsschule1. If you are combining several licences – say SBF Binnen plus a radio certificate – and do not want a subscription, Boatpass fits, because all five catalogues sit in one app.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I prepare for the German boating licence entirely with an app?',
    a: 'The theory, yes. The official question catalogue is public and no theory course is required – you register directly with the examination board. No app replaces the practical exam: knots and manoeuvres have to be practised on the water, usually with a boating school.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are the questions in these apps the real exam questions?',
    a: 'In every app compared here, yes. The catalogues for SBF Binnen, SBF See and the radio certificates are published officially, among others via elwis.de, and serious apps reproduce them one to one. Still check that the app states the current catalogue version.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Free or paid – is the difference worth it?',
    a: 'The free apps contain the complete question catalogue and are enough for pure memorisation. Paid versions typically add explanations for each answer, exam simulations on original papers, mistake training and progress statistics. If you want to understand rather than memorise, that is worth the money – if not, save it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need an internet connection to study?',
    a: 'Most apps work offline, in some cases only after buying the full version. Boatpass, SBF-Fragen, Bootsprüfung, the Goritz apps and the Wimmer apps work without a connection. With Bootspruefung.de, full offline availability is a Pro feature; with Sailbyte, SBF See and Binnen work offline while SKS does not.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are these apps available for iPhone?',
    a: 'Almost all of them. Bootspruefung.de, Bootsprüfung, Bootsschule1, SBF-Fragen, SBF Binnen by Ralf Goritz, Sailbyte and Boatpass (since October 2026) are available for Android and iOS, SBF See by Ralf Goritz for iOS only. Only the free Wimmer apps are limited to Android.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does the German boating licence cost in total?',
    a: 'The app is the smallest item. Expect official examination fees of roughly €100 to €190 depending on the licence, plus boating school costs if you take that route. Our costs page breaks it down.',
  },
];

const relatedLinks = [
  { href: '/en/sbf-coastal-app/', label: 'SBF See apps compared' },
  { href: '/en/sbf-inland-app/', label: 'SBF Binnen apps compared' },
  { href: '/en/radio-certificate-app/', label: 'Radio certificate apps for UBI, SRC and LRC' },
  { href: '/en/sbf-app-free/', label: 'Free boating licence apps – what is actually free' },
  { href: '/en/sbf-costs/', label: 'What does the German boating licence cost?' },
  { href: '/en/blog/sbf-app-vs-boating-school/', label: 'App or boating school – what pays off?' },
];
---

<AppLandingPage
  lang="en"
  title="German boating licence apps compared 2026"
  description="Looking for a German boating licence app? Ten apps honestly compared on price, licences and ratings from both stores – from Bootspruefung.de to Boatpass."
  altUrl="https://boatpass.de/sbf-app/"
  path="/sbf-app/"
  breadcrumbName="Boating licence apps compared"
  badge="Vendor comparison 2026"
  h1="German boating licence apps compared"
  heroIntro="Ten learning apps for the German Sportbootführerschein and the radio certificates – with real prices, ratings from Google Play and the App Store, and licence coverage. Including an honest note on where our own app is not the best choice."
  answer="Ten widely used learning apps matter for the German boating licence: Bootspruefung.de is the market leader with around 27,000 store ratings, the Wimmer apps for SBF See and Binnen are completely free, the apps by Ralf Goritz have the most carefully built learning mechanic, SBF-Fragen comes from publisher Delius Klasing, Bootsschule1 belongs to a complete course including practical training, Sailbyte runs on a subscription, Bootsprüfung is the newest provider, and Boatpass bundles five catalogues in one app without a subscription."
  apps={LEARNING_APPS}
  tableCaption="Ratings from Google Play and the German App Store, prices and features from vendor websites – sorted alphabetically."
  androidHeading="Boating licence apps for Android"
  androidParagraphs={[
    'On Android, nine of the ten apps are available; only SBF See by Ralf Goritz is exclusive to iPhone and iPad. If you only need one licence and do not want to pay, the two apps by Matthias Wimmer are the obvious pick: <strong>Sportbootführerschein Binnen</strong> and <strong>Sportbootführerschein See 2023</strong>, both very highly rated, entirely free, ad-free and without tracking.',
    'If you need several licences it gets messy: with Wimmer, Goritz and Sailbyte you install a separate app per licence, each with its own progress. Bootspruefung.de, Bootsprüfung, SBF-Fragen and Boatpass keep everything in one install.',
    'Check the catalogue version before you download. The official catalogues are updated periodically, and an app with outdated questions prepares you badly.',
  ]}
  iosHeading="Boating licence apps for iPhone and iPad"
  iosParagraphs={[
    'On iOS the choice is wide too: <strong>Bootspruefung.de</strong>, <strong>SBF-Fragen</strong> from publisher Delius Klasing, <strong>Bootsprüfung</strong>, <strong>Bootsschule1</strong>, <strong>Boatpass</strong> and the two apps by <strong>Ralf Goritz</strong> are on the App Store. Goritz’s SBF See is available only there; it is the most-rated coastal-only app and shows every navigation task as an animation.',
    'The free Wimmer apps are Android only, while Sailbyte has had all three of its apps on the App Store since September 2026. <strong>Boatpass has been on the App Store since October 2026</strong> and covers all five licences there, just like on Android, including the radio bundle for UBI, SRC and LRC. Purchases only apply to the store you bought in, though – switching from Android to iPhone means unlocking again.',
    'Watch out for the name twin: the App Store also lists an unrelated app called “BoatPass” from a US boat rental service in Florida. Our study app is the one by <strong>Marius Gehler</strong> in the Education category.',
  ]}
  strengths={[
    'Five catalogues – SBF See, SBF Binnen, UBI, SRC and LRC – in a single app',
    'One-off purchase instead of a subscription, permanent access',
    'Exam simulation under real exam conditions',
    'Mistake training: repeat exactly the questions you got wrong',
    'Progress broken down by topic area',
    'Study offline – works without an internet connection',
  ]}
  limitations={[
    'No SKS, no Lake Constance licence, no FKN pyrotechnics certificate',
    'Purchases apply per store – no transfer between Android and iPhone',
    'Far younger and far less reviewed than Bootspruefung.de or SBF-Fragen',
    'No companion online course in the browser',
    'Does not replace practical training with a boating school',
  ]}
  faqs={faqs}
  relatedLinks={relatedLinks}
>
  <section slot="after-table" style="margin-bottom:48px;">
    <h2 class="content-section-title" style="margin-bottom:16px;">How we compared</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#4B5563; line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:12px;">
      The table shows every learning app with at least 500 ratings in either store. On top of that come Sailbyte as the only subscription model and Bootsprüfung by PriorApps, because this app ranks at the top in searches for “Bootsführerschein App”. Boatpass, as our own app, is always included and marked accordingly.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#4B5563; line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:12px;">
      Ratings and download figures come straight from Google Play and the German App Store; prices and features come from the vendors’ websites and store descriptions. We show the two stores separately because they have different numbers of ratings. An average built on a few dozen ratings, as with Boatpass or Bootsprüfung, says less than one built on several thousand.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#4B5563; line-height:1.75; margin-bottom:12px;">
      The links to stores and vendors are not affiliate links. When prices or features change, we update the data; the date is shown below the table.
    </p>
  </section>
</AppLandingPage>
